menu "Loxone 1-Wire bridge"

    config LOXONE_ONEWIRE
        bool "Enable the Loxone 1-Wire bridge"
        default n
        help
            After a successful HomeKey authentication the device presents a
            virtual Dallas DS1990A iButton on a 1-Wire bus for a short time.
            A Loxone 1-Wire Extension (or any other 1-Wire master) sees this as
            an iButton being presented and can use it to grant access.

            The feature is configured at runtime on the "Loxone" page of the
            web UI. The options below only provide the initial values.

    if LOXONE_ONEWIRE

        config LOXONE_ONEWIRE_DEFAULT_ENABLED
            bool "Start the bridge before it was configured in the web UI"
            default y
            help
                Initial state of the bridge until the settings were saved once.

        config LOXONE_ONEWIRE_GPIO
            int "Default 1-Wire GPIO pin"
            default 27 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32
            default 4
            range 0 48
            help
                Pin connected to the DATA line of the 1-Wire master. It must be
                output capable (not GPIO34-39 on the ESP32) and needs an
                external 4.7k pull-up resistor to 3.3V. The pin is driven
                open-drain.

        config LOXONE_ONEWIRE_ACTIVE_MS
            int "Default time the iButton stays on the bus after a tap (ms)"
            default 3000
            range 500 4500
            help
                Loxone polls the bus roughly once per second, so 3000 ms gives
                two to three poll cycles. Capped at 4500 ms because the bus task
                busy-polls the pin while active and would otherwise trip the
                idle task watchdog (default 5 s).

        config LOXONE_ONEWIRE_TASK_CORE
            int "CPU core of the bus task"
            depends on !FREERTOS_UNICORE
            range 0 1
            default 1
            help
                The task runs at high priority and busy-polls the pin while an
                iButton is presented. Pick the core that is less loaded.

    endif

endmenu
